        "original_id": "56c71439-0b45-5dcf-9a7a-005aea5fe840",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Sunday Driver, Madrugada, MonstrO\n- People: Bevan Davies, Kyle Sanders, Juan Montoya, Charlie Suarez\n- Music scenes: UK Steampunk scene\n- Albums: Madrugada\n- Events: band split announcement, final concert\n\nFacts:\n- On 21 January 2008, Madrugada released the album \"Madrugada\" and announced that the band would split after one last tour.\n- On 15 November 2008, Madrugada performed its final concert.\n- In 2009, Sunday Driver became popular within the UK Steampunk scene.\n- MonstrO is an alternative band composed of Bevan Davies, Kyle Sanders, Juan Montoya, and Charlie Suarez.\n- Bevan Davies had previously been the drummer for Still Rain, Danzig, and Bloodsimple before joining MonstrO.\n- Kyle Sanders had previously been the bassist for Bloodsimple, Medication, and Skrew before joining MonstrO.\n- Juan Montoya had previously been the guitarist for Torche before joining MonstrO.\n- Charlie Suarez had previously been associated with Sunday Driver before joining MonstrO.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
